<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MixedGearVisualFix — manual pair exceptions.
  Edit this file, no rebuild needed. Rules override the built-in family matrix.

  ELEMENTS
    <Ban .../>    this glove/boot may NEVER appear with this body armor
    <Allow .../>  force-allow a pair the family matrix would ban (Ban always beats Allow)

  ATTRIBUTES (all optional, all accept comma-separated lists)
    item / items          glove or boot StringId(s)
    itemMesh / itemMeshes glove or boot mesh name(s)  (the mesh="..." attribute in the armor mod's items XML)
    body / bodies         body armor StringId(s)
    bodyMesh / bodyMeshes body armor mesh name(s)

  Omitting the body side = the rule applies against EVERY body armor.
  Omitting the item side = the rule applies to EVERY glove/boot worn with that body.

  EXAMPLES (remove the surrounding comment markers to activate):

  1) One specific glove never with one specific body armor:
     <Ban item="eoe_splinted_gloves_1" body="imperial_scale_armor" />

  2) One glove banned with several body armors:
     <Ban item="eoe_splinted_gloves_1" bodies="imperial_scale_armor,imperial_lamellar_armor,decorated_scale_armor" />

  3) Several boots banned with one body armor:
     <Ban items="leather_boots,strapped_leather_boots,ragged_boots" body="ta_kolontar_1" />

  4) Ban by mesh (catches every item variant sharing that mesh):
     <Ban itemMesh="eoe_plategloves_1" bodyMesh="anno_gambeson_a" />

  5) A completely broken boot — ban it with everything:
     <Ban item="some_broken_boots" />

  6) Force-allow a pair the family matrix blocks:
     <Allow item="eoe_splinted_gloves_1" body="imperial_padded_cloth" />
-->
<CompatibilityExceptions>

</CompatibilityExceptions>